"--\n"
"The SMTP port. The default value depends on the configuration. The port 25 "
"is used as default when `ssl` is disabled. This port continues to be used "
"primarily for SMTP relaying. SMTP relaying is the transmission of email from "
"email server to email server. The port 587 is the default port when `ssl` is "
"enabled. It ensures that email is submitted securely. Note that the port 465 "
"may be used by SMTP servers, however, IANA has reassigned a new service to "
"this port, and it should no longer be used for SMTP communications.\n"
"\n"
